body:
Indeed, rendering on mobile we do a divide by 2 on the output to make better use of the RGB10 range. There is a multiply by 2 in tonemapping. However with blend multiply, this is the wrong thing to do.

I'm not sure if your fix does the right thing, it also will likely be wrong if HDR output is enabled and we use an RGB16F buffer even on the mobile renderer. 

The real fix is to skip the divide by 2 in the scene output IF `blend_mult` is used.
So basically skip over ([scene_forward_mobile.glsl#L2426](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/forward_mobile/scene_forward_mobile.glsl#L2426)):
```
	// On mobile we use a UNORM buffer with 10bpp which results in a range from 0.0 - 1.0 resulting in HDR breaking
	// We divide by sc_luminance_multiplier to support a range from 0.0 - 2.0 both increasing precision on bright and darker images
	out_color.rgb = out_color.rgb / sc_luminance_multiplier();
```
